      "writtenOn": "2022-10-27T12:09:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I checked this again, it looks like these asserts are ignored in test.\n\nActually I want to make sure that the string returned by the API is a NULL-terminated C string. There\u0027s a conversion below to change the type to string before passing it to the host. So testing in host somehow hides this problem.\n\nWhen I tested this properly on local, the return of `AVmPayload_getApkContentsPath()` is `/mnt/apk/\\x02\\x00`, instead of `/mnt/apk/\\x00`.\n\nIf we want to return a static string `/mnt/apk/\\x00`, maybe we can create a c layer between the header and rust_ffi and get the static string directly from aidl c interface.\n\nOr we can make an API similar to what Andrew did to write the param. Then we need to add a method to get path length, so that clients can allocate enough memory before calling `getApkContentsPath(char* path)`.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "3b0fceb8_283b8a62",
